# Cline Project Intelligence for Magics

## Project Patterns
- Implement efficient Gaussian Belief Propagation (GBP) for path planning
- Design modular component architecture with clearly defined interfaces
- Enforce type safety across Rust-Python boundary
- Balance performance with reinforcement learning flexibility
- Leverage Bevy ECS architecture for simulation components
- Maintain clean separation between core simulation and Python API

## Coding Conventions
- Follow Rust idioms for core simulation code
- Use snake_case for variables and functions
- Use SCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE for constants
- Apply PyO3 attribute macros consistently for Python exports
- Keep Python-facing API simple and Pythonic
- Document API boundary thoroughly
- Use strong typing for API parameters with clear validation
- Prefer immutable data structures where possible

## GBP Implementation Guidelines
- Optimize message passing for critical paths
- Ensure numerical stability in belief updates
- Minimize computational complexity in factor calculations
- Support both system-wide and per-agent factor weights
- Maintain clear separation between variables and factors
- Implement efficient state extraction for external observation
- Use fixed point optimization for performance-critical areas

## Python API Guidelines
- Design for OpenAI Gym compatibility
- Provide clean error propagation from Rust to Python
- Minimize data copying across language boundary
- Create intuitive action and observation spaces
- Support reinforcement learning workflows
- Ensure thread safety in step-based execution
- Implement efficient serialization between languages

## Optimization Strategies
- Cache factor graph state for API access
- Optimize state extraction for minimal overhead
- Use batch operations for weight updates
- Implement efficient step synchronization
- Leverage Rust's zero-cost abstractions
- Profile both Rust and Python sides of the boundary
- Minimize allocations during hot paths

## Documentation Requirements
- Document all Python-exposed functions thoroughly
- Explain factor graph weight parameters and effects
- Include examples for OpenAI Gym integration
- Document reward function implementations
- Provide clear API versioning
- Include performance considerations
- Add tutorials for reinforcement learning setup

## Testing Approach
- Unit test core simulation components
- Test Python bindings separately
- Create integration tests for end-to-end workflows
- Benchmark API performance at various agent counts
- Test with different reinforcement learning algorithms
- Validate numerical stability with various weight configurations
- Test thread safety and concurrent access

## Performance Monitoring
- Profile message passing efficiency
- Measure serialization overhead
- Track API call latency
- Monitor memory usage during simulation steps
- Benchmark step execution time
- Compare performance with and without API active
- Profile Python GIL impact

## Research Directions
- Optimize factor weights through reinforcement learning
- Discover emergent multi-agent behaviors
- Benchmark against other path planning approaches
- Explore adaptive weight adjustment strategies
- Investigate scaling laws with increasing agent count
- Study communication patterns in multi-agent scenarios
- Research transfer learning between simulation and reality

